Summary of what landed:
- **`src/lib/server/atomic.ts`**: added sync `atomicRenameSync` so the rotator opts into atomic-rename semantics without reaching into `node:fs` directly.
- **`src/lib/server/generation.ts`**: new `eventsLogPath`, `readEventsLogSync`, `EventsLogEntry`, `EVENTS_LOG_BASENAME` (`.generation-events.ndjson`), `EVENTS_LOG_ROTATE_BYTES_DEFAULT` (5 MB), and `__setEventsLogRotateBytesForTesting`. `GenerationListener` now `(event, seq) => void`; `GenerationRun` gained `lastSeq` + `eventSeqs`. `emit()` synchronously appends `{ seq, timestamp, event }` to the ndjson **before** notifying listeners, then `statSync` and rotates via `atomicRenameSync` past 5 MB. Resume seeds `lastSeq` from the existing log; fresh runs truncate.
- **`src/app/api/courses/generate/stream/[id]/route.ts`**: parses `Last-Event-ID` (precedence) and `?from=`, sync replay from ndjson inside `ReadableStream#start`, race-free backstop over `run.eventSeqs[0..snapshotLen)`, listener dedupes on `seq <= lastReplayedSeq`. Each frame is `id: <seq>\nevent: <type>\ndata: <json>\n\n`. Single `console.warn` per replay if malformed lines were skipped.
- **Tests**: 7 new tests under `describe('persistent generation events ndjson + SSE replay (US-138)')`.

Verified: `npm run typecheck` clean, `npm test` 750/750.
